    "updated_at": "2017-09-20T11:57:47Z",
    "body": "#### Alternative\r\nJust in case the `file:` issue raised by @GreLI comes up again, an alternative with all the benefits and a less implicit mechanism could be:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<!-- loaded externally on top of the head -->\r\n<script type=\"module-namespaces\" src=\"/mjs.json\"></script>\r\n``` \r\n\r\nThis still grants the site owner is the only one with write access to such file and a local/file based application could point at an actual file in the folder via relative path.\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
