    "created_at": "2017-09-20T13:02:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-20T13:02:07Z",
    "body": "Thanks for this contribution. We're currently tracking this problem at https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2640, which probably isn't named in a very searchable way; maybe I can fix that. However, let's consolidate discussion there (feel free to link to this proposal from there).\r\n\r\nIn general we're not very interested in adding module-specific solutions to this general problem of mapping resource specifiers to actual URLs; we want to solve this for all resources. And we definitely shouldn't emulate the huge pain that is favicon.ico behavior. Keeping the information in a separate file is also problematic as it prevents preload scanning from working, at least on first load. But some manifest might indeed make sense, probably inline in the document. As #2640 states, we'd like to see what people come up with in service workers first.\r\n\r\nLet me close this, and please feel free to continue discussion in #2640. I will rename #2640 and add a quick summary of recommended reading at the top of it.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
