    "updated_at": "2017-09-20T13:08:15Z",
    "body": "I've searched a little and indeed couldn't find that issue, I was surprised myself there was no discussion going on.\r\n\r\nI will link this documentation there after reading what's been discussed already, however, I'd like to clarify this point:\r\n\r\n> we definitely shouldn't emulate the huge pain that is favicon.ico behavior\r\n\r\nthe `favicon.ico` case has been mentioned not to necessarily copy it, rather to underline that a single extra request has never been an issue for the last 20+ years of Web so that having a convention that loads a single \"_manifest_\" upfront shouldn't be seen as a stopper 'cause loading a file upfront has never been a stopper for the web.\r\n\r\nI hope I've better clarified the metaphore/reason I've put favicon.ico on the plate.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
