    "body": "> a single extra request has never been an issue for the last 20+ years of Web\r\n\r\nThe favicon.ico request has been a _huge_ issue for the web; why do you think it's been a success? Just the first Google result for \"favicon.ico bad\" for me is this informative article: http://techblog.wimgodden.be/2011/02/22/how-a-bad-favicon-ico-can-cause-a-lot-of-trouble/ . (Obviously some of its points are favicon specific, but several of the biggest problems it points out are for any such request.)",
