    "created_at": "2017-09-20T14:33:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-09-20T14:33:55Z",
    "body": "@WebReflection the production tree has shared dependencies, in the way chunks share dependencies (eg shared-core.js, shared-section.js, current-chunk.js). I'm by no means advocating a development module tree in production. Chunks can have more than 1 layer of depth, which would correspond to a similar ES module production workflow, and hence preloading need. This is exploring production semantics to edges yes, but semantics are there - we should support their optimization.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
